     1→# ADR-013: Extension UI
     2→
     3→**Status:** Proposed
     4→**Date:** 2026-01-30
     5→**Decision Makers:** TBD
     6→
     7→---
     8→
     9→## Context
    10→
    11→The extension needs a UI to show recording state, errors, and provide access to settings. VS Code offers several UI options: status bar, sidebar panels, webviews, notifications, and quick picks.
    12→
    13→## Decision Drivers
    14→
    15→- **Simplicity**: Minimal UI footprint
    16→- **Non-intrusive**: Don't distract from coding
    17→- **Discoverability**: Users can find settings easily
    18→- **Feedback**: Clear indication of recording state
    19→
    20→## Decision
    21→
    22→**Status bar item only** for MVP. No panels, sidebars, or custom webviews for UI.
    23→
    24→```
    25→┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    26→│  VS CODE WINDOW                                                              │
    27→│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
    28→│  │                         EDITOR / TERMINAL                            │    │
    29→│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
    30→│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
    31→│  │ main.ts   Ln 42, Col 12   UTF-8       $(mic) Voice        Spaces: 2 │    │
    32→│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
    33→│                                          ▲                                   │
    34→│                                          └── STATUS BAR ITEM                 │
    35→└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    36→```
    37→
    38→## Status Bar States
    39→
    40→| State | Icon | Text | Background | Tooltip |
    41→|-------|------|------|------------|---------|
    42→| Idle | `$(mic)` | Voice | default | "Press Ctrl+Shift+D to dictate" |
    43→| Recording | `$(pulse)` | 0:03 | warning (yellow) | "Recording... (ESC to cancel)" |
    44→| Processing | `$(sync~spin)` | — | default | "Processing..." |
    45→| Error | `$(error)` | Voice | error (red) | "Error: {message}" |
    46→| Disconnected | `$(mic-off)` | Voice | default | "Not connected (click to configure)" |
    47→
    48→```
    49→┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    50→│  VISUAL STATES                                                  │
    51→├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    52→│                                                                 │
    53→│  ┌──────────────┐                                              │
    54→│  │ $(mic) Voice │  Idle - ready to record                      │
    55→│  └──────────────┘                                              │
    56→│                                                                 │
    57→│  ┌──────────────┐                                              │
    58→│  │ $(pulse) 0:03│  Recording - yellow background, timer        │
    59→│  └──────────────┘                                              │
    60→│                                                                 │
    61→│  ┌──────────────┐                                              │
    62→│  │$(sync~spin)  │  Processing - spinning icon                  │
    63→│  └──────────────┘                                              │
    64→│                                                                 │
    65→│  ┌──────────────┐                                              │
    66→│  │$(error) Voice│  Error - red background                      │
    67→│  └──────────────┘                                              │
    68→│                                                                 │
    69→│  ┌──────────────┐                                              │
    70→│  │$(mic-off)    │  Disconnected - grayed out                   │
    71→│  └──────────────┘                                              │
    72→│                                                                 │
    73→└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    74→```
    75→
    76→## Click Actions
    77→
    78→| Current State | Click Action |
    79→|---------------|-------------|
    80→| Idle | Show quick pick menu |
    81→| Recording | Cancel recording |
    82→| Processing | No action (wait) |
    83→| Error | Show error details, offer retry |
    84→| Disconnected | Open setup wizard |
    85→
    86→## Quick Pick Menu
    87→
    88→When clicking the status bar in idle state:
    89→
    90→```
    91→┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    92→│  Voice Code                                                     │
    93→├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    94→│  $(gear)  Settings              Configure Voice Code           │
    95→│  $(plug)  Test Connection       Check backend status           │
    96→│  $(mic)   Test Microphone       Record a test clip             │
    97→│  $(book)  Vocabulary            Manage custom terms            │
    98→│  $(sign-out) Sign Out           Disconnect account             │
    99→└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   100→```
   101→
   102→## Implementation
   103→
   104→### StatusBarUI Class
   105→
   106→```typescript
   107→import * as vscode from 'vscode';
   108→
   109→type UIState = 'idle' | 'recording' | 'processing' | 'error' | 'disconnected';
   110→
   111→class StatusBarUI {
   112→    private item: vscode.StatusBarItem;
   113→    private recordingTimer: NodeJS.Timeout | null = null;
   114→    private recordingStart: number = 0;
   115→    private currentState: UIState = 'idle';
   116→    private errorMessage: string = '';
   117→
   118→    constructor() {
   119→        this.item = vscode.window.createStatusBarItem(
   120→            vscode.StatusBarAlignment.Right,
   121→            100
   122→        );
   123→        this.item.command = 'voicecode.statusBarClick';
   124→        this.setIdle();
   125→        this.item.show();
   126→    }
   127→
   128→    getState(): UIState {
   129→        return this.currentState;
   130→    }
   131→
   132→    setIdle(): void {
   133→        this.currentState = 'idle';
   134→        this.stopTimer();
   135→        this.item.text = '$(mic) Voice';
   136→        this.item.tooltip = 'Voice Code - Press Ctrl+Shift+D to dictate';
   137→        this.item.backgroundColor = undefined;
   138→    }
   139→
   140→    setRecording(): void {
   141→        this.currentState = 'recording';
   142→        this.recordingStart = Date.now();
   143→        this.updateRecordingTime();
   144→        this.item.tooltip = 'Recording... (ESC to cancel, click to stop)';
   145→        this.item.backgroundColor = new vscode.ThemeColor(
   146→            'statusBarItem.warningBackground'
   147→        );
   148→
   149→        this.recordingTimer = setInterval(() => {
   150→            this.updateRecordingTime();
   151→        }, 1000);
   152→    }
   153→
   154→    setProcessing(): void {
   155→        this.currentState = 'processing';
   156→        this.stopTimer();
   157→        this.item.text = '$(sync~spin)';
   158→        this.item.tooltip = 'Processing transcription...';
   159→        this.item.backgroundColor = undefined;
   160→    }
   161→
   162→    setError(message: string): void {
   163→        this.currentState = 'error';
   164→        this.errorMessage = message;
   165→        this.stopTimer();
   166→        this.item.text = '$(error) Voice';
   167→        this.item.tooltip = `Error: ${message} (click for options)`;
   168→        this.item.backgroundColor = new vscode.ThemeColor(
   169→            'statusBarItem.errorBackground'
   170→        );
   171→
   172→        // Auto-clear error after 10 seconds
   173→        setTimeout(() => {
   174→            if (this.currentState === 'error') {
   175→                this.setIdle();
   176→            }
   177→        }, 10000);
   178→    }
   179→
   180→    setDisconnected(): void {
   181→        this.currentState = 'disconnected';
   182→        this.stopTimer();
   183→        this.item.text = '$(mic-off) Voice';
   184→        this.item.tooltip = 'Not connected - click to configure';
   185→        this.item.backgroundColor = undefined;
   186→    }
   187→
   188→    private updateRecordingTime(): void {
   189→        const elapsed = Math.floor((Date.now() - this.recordingStart) / 1000);
   190→        const mins = Math.floor(elapsed / 60);
   191→        const secs = elapsed % 60;
   192→        this.item.text = `$(pulse) ${mins}:${secs.toString().padStart(2, '0')}`;
   193→    }
   194→
   195→    private stopTimer(): void {
   196→        if (this.recordingTimer) {
   197→            clearInterval(this.recordingTimer);
   198→            this.recordingTimer = null;
   199→        }
   200→    }
   201→
   202→    dispose(): void {
   203→        this.stopTimer();
   204→        this.item.dispose();
   205→    }
   206→}
   207→```
   208→
   209→### Click Handler
   210→
   211→```typescript
   212→async function handleStatusBarClick(ui: StatusBarUI): Promise<void> {
   213→    const state = ui.getState();
   214→
   215→    switch (state) {
   216→        case 'idle':
   217→            await showMainMenu();
   218→            break;
   219→
   220→        case 'recording':
   221→            // Cancel current recording
   222→            vscode.commands.executeCommand('voicecode.cancel');
   223→            break;
   224→
   225→        case 'error':
   226→            await showErrorMenu();
   227→            break;
   228→
   229→        case 'disconnected':
   230→            await showSetupWizard();
   231→            break;
   232→
   233→        case 'processing':
   234→            // Do nothing - wait for completion
   235→            break;
   236→    }
   237→}
   238→
   239→async function showMainMenu(): Promise<void> {
   240→    const items: vscode.QuickPickItem[] = [
   241→        {
   242→            label: '$(gear) Settings',
   243→            description: 'Configure Voice Code'
   244→        },
   245→        {
   246→            label: '$(plug) Test Connection',
   247→            description: 'Check backend status'
   248→        },
   249→        {
   250→            label: '$(mic) Test Microphone',
   251→            description: 'Record a short test clip'
   252→        },
   253→        {
   254→            label: '$(book) Vocabulary',
   255→            description: 'Manage custom terms'
   256→        },
   257→        {
   258→            label: '$(sign-out) Sign Out',
   259→            description: 'Disconnect your account'
   260→        },
   261→    ];
   262→
   263→    const selected = await vscode.window.showQuickPick(items, {
   264→        placeHolder: 'Voice Code'
   265→    });
   266→
   267→    if (!selected) return;
   268→
   269→    switch (selected.label) {
   270→        case '$(gear) Settings':
   271→            vscode.commands.executeCommand(
   272→                'workbench.action.openSettings',
   273→                'voicecode'
   274→            );
   275→            break;
   276→
   277→        case '$(plug) Test Connection':
   278→            vscode.commands.executeCommand('voicecode.testConnection');
   279→            break;
   280→
   281→        case '$(mic) Test Microphone':
   282→            vscode.commands.executeCommand('voicecode.testMicrophone');
   283→            break;
   284→
   285→        case '$(book) Vocabulary':
   286→            vscode.commands.executeCommand('voicecode.manageVocabulary');
   287→            break;
   288→
   289→        case '$(sign-out) Sign Out':
   290→            vscode.commands.executeCommand('voicecode.signOut');
   291→            break;
   292→    }
   293→}
   294→
   295→async function showErrorMenu(): Promise<void> {
   296→    const items: vscode.QuickPickItem[] = [
   297→        { label: '$(refresh) Retry Connection', description: 'Try connecting again' },
   298→        { label: '$(gear) Check Settings', description: 'Verify configuration' },
   299→        { label: '$(output) View Logs', description: 'Open output channel' },
   300→    ];
   301→
   302→    const selected = await vscode.window.showQuickPick(items, {
   303→        placeHolder: 'Connection Error'
   304→    });
   305→
   306→    if (!selected) return;
   307→
   308→    switch (selected.label) {
   309→        case '$(refresh) Retry Connection':
   310→            vscode.commands.executeCommand('voicecode.reconnect');
   311→            break;
   312→
   313→        case '$(gear) Check Settings':
   314→            vscode.commands.executeCommand(
   315→                'workbench.action.openSettings',
   316→                'voicecode.backend'
   317→            );
   318→            break;
   319→
   320→        case '$(output) View Logs':
   321→            vscode.commands.executeCommand('voicecode.showOutput');
   322→            break;
   323→    }
   324→}
   325→```
   326→
   327→### Vocabulary Quick Pick
   328→
   329→Simple inline editing via quick pick:
   330→
   331→```typescript
   332→async function showVocabularyMenu(): Promise<void> {
   333→    const vocab = await getVocabulary(); // From backend
   334→
   335→    const items: vscode.QuickPickItem[] = [
   336→        { label: '$(add) Add Term', description: 'Add a new vocabulary term' },
   337→        { label: '', kind: vscode.QuickPickItemKind.Separator },
   338→        ...vocab.map(term => ({
   339→            label: term,
   340→            description: 'Click to remove'
   341→        }))
   342→    ];
   343→
   344→    const selected = await vscode.window.showQuickPick(items, {
   345→        placeHolder: 'Vocabulary - technical terms for better accuracy'
   346→    });
   347→
   348→    if (!selected) return;
   349→
   350→    if (selected.label === '$(add) Add Term') {
   351→        const term = await vscode.window.showInputBox({
   352→            prompt: 'Enter technical term (e.g., "FastAPI", "kubectl")',
   353→            placeHolder: 'Term'
   354→        });
   355→        if (term) {
   356→            await addVocabularyTerm(term);
   357→            vscode.window.showInformationMessage(`Added "${term}" to vocabulary`);
   358→        }
   359→    } else if (selected.label) {
   360→        const confirm = await vscode.window.showWarningMessage(
   361→            `Remove "${selected.label}" from vocabulary?`,
   362→            'Remove',
   363→            'Cancel'
   364→        );
   365→        if (confirm === 'Remove') {
   366→            await removeVocabularyTerm(selected.label);
   367→        }
   368→    }
   369→}
