   597→### Integration with Audio Pipeline
   598→
   599→```typescript
   600→class DictationController {
   601→    private modeRegistry: ActivationModeRegistry;
   602→    private audioCapture: AudioCapture;
   603→    private wsClient: WebSocketClient;
   604→    private textManager: InterimTextManager;
   605→
   606→    constructor(
   607→        config: ActivationConfig,
   608→        audioCapture: AudioCapture,
   609→        wsClient: WebSocketClient,
   610→        textManager: InterimTextManager
   611→    ) {
   612→        this.audioCapture = audioCapture;
   613→        this.wsClient = wsClient;
   614→        this.textManager = textManager;
   615→
   616→        // Set up mode registry with callbacks
   617→        this.modeRegistry = new ActivationModeRegistry();
   618→        this.modeRegistry.setCallbacks({
   619→            onRecordingStart: () => this.startRecording(),
   620→            onRecordingStop: () => this.stopRecording(),
   621→            onRecordingCancel: () => this.cancelRecording(),
   622→            onError: (error) => this.handleError(error)
   623→        });
   624→
   625→        // Activate configured mode
   626→        this.modeRegistry.switchMode(config.mode);
   627→    }
   628→
   629→    private async startRecording(): Promise<void> {
   630→        // Update UI
   631→        this.showRecordingIndicator();
   632→
   633→        // Start audio capture
   634→        await this.audioCapture.start();
   635→
   636→        // Open WebSocket connection
   637→        await this.wsClient.connect();
   638→
   639→        // Stream audio chunks
   640→        this.audioCapture.onData((chunk) => {
   641→            this.wsClient.sendAudio(chunk);
   642→        });
   643→    }
   644→
   645→    private async stopRecording(): Promise<void> {
   646→        // Stop audio capture
   647→        await this.audioCapture.stop();
   648→
   649→        // Signal end of audio to server
   650→        this.wsClient.sendStop();
   651→
   652→        // Update UI
   653→        this.showProcessingIndicator();
   654→    }
   655→
   656→    private async cancelRecording(): Promise<void> {
   657→        // Stop audio capture
   658→        await this.audioCapture.stop();
   659→
   660→        // Close WebSocket without processing
   661→        this.wsClient.close();
   662→
   663→        // Clean up any interim text
   664→        await this.textManager.cancel(vscode.window.activeTextEditor!);
   665→
   666→        // Update UI
   667→        this.hideIndicator();
   668→    }
   669→
   670→    private handleError(error: Error): void {
   671→        vscode.window.showErrorMessage(`Dictation error: ${error.message}`);
   672→        this.cancelRecording();
   673→    }
   674→
   675→    /**
   676→     * Switch activation mode at runtime.
   677→     */
   678→    setMode(mode: string): void {
   679→        this.modeRegistry.switchMode(mode);
   680→        vscode.commands.executeCommand(
   681→            'setContext',
   682→            'voicecode.mode',
   683→            mode
   684→        );
   685→    }
   686→}
   687→```
   688→
   689→## Consequences
   690→
   691→### Positive
   692→- **Intuitive default**: Push-to-talk is familiar to most users
   693→- **Flexible architecture**: Easy to add new modes without changing core logic
   694→- **User choice**: Different modes suit different workflows
   695→- **Accident prevention**: Minimum duration prevents accidental activations
   696→
   697→### Negative
   698→- **VS Code keybinding limitations**: Key up detection requires workarounds
   699→- **Mode complexity**: Users must understand mode differences
   700→- **Testing burden**: Each mode needs thorough testing
   701→
   702→### VS Code Keybinding Workaround
   703→
   704→VS Code doesn't natively support key-up events. Options:
   705→
   706→1. **WebView bridge**: Handle key events in WebView, forward to extension
   707→2. **Keyboard monitoring**: Use native module (platform-specific)
   708→3. **Timer-based**: Treat long press differently than short press
   709→
   710→For MVP, use WebView bridge since we already have a WebView for audio capture:
   711→
   712→```typescript
   713→// WebView script
   714→document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
   715→    if (e.ctrlKey && e.shiftKey && e.key === 'd') {
   716→        vscode.postMessage({ type: 'keydown', key: 'activation' });
   717→    }
   718→});
   719→
   720→document.addEventListener('keyup', (e) => {
   721→    if (e.key === 'd') {
   722→        vscode.postMessage({ type: 'keyup', key: 'activation' });
   723→    }
   724→});
   725→```
